<?xpacket begin="ï»¿" id="W5M0MpCehiHzreSzNTczkc9d"?>
<x:xmpmeta xmlns:x="adobe:ns:meta/">
  <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#">
    <rdf:Description xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" rdf:about="">
      <dc:title>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Maps</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;Catra learns how to navigate the Whispering Woods.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;â€”&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;â€œYou have done some bad things, dearie.â€&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The fur on Catraâ€™s spine stood up and she furrowed her brow. â€œYeah, I know, okay? No need to rub it in,â€ she grumbled. She sipped her tea and turned her gaze toward the wall.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;â€œBut do you think the trees are scared of you? Angry at you? The Woods have been around far longer than even Madame Razz. The scars of this war that you and Adora fought are not the first, and they will not be the last.â€ Razz sipped her own tea, then breathed a deep sigh. â€œI must have taught you this lesson a thousand times already, dearie. Magic does not hold petty grudges! Magic is simply there, waiting for you to decide how to treat it. Will you try to destroy it? Control it? Or will you let it into your heart?â€&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
      <dc:creator>
        <rdf:Seq>
          <rdf:li>strongcat</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Seq>
      </dc:creator>
      <dc:subject>
        <rdf:Bag>
          <rdf:li>Fanworks</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>She-Ra and the Princesses of Power (2018)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Adora/Catra (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Catra (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Adora (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Razz (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Melog (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
